!!! archon/cli/scanner-cli.mat
!!! The Archon command-line scanner.
!!!
!!! Usage:  archon <path> [<path> ...]
!!!
!!! Each argument is a target. The kind is taken from the path's extension, the
!!! matching rules are drawn from the catalog, and the target is scanned into
!!! findings and a machine-readable report line. Reading uses the shared runtime
!!! (`ny.lang.system` arguments, `ny.lang.io` file reads), so the same page runs
!!! under the interpreter today and, later, on the Anomalous ABI.

book archon.cli.scanner

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from ny.lang.text
read everything from ny.lang.system
read everything from ny.lang.io
read everything from archon.model.target
read everything from archon.model.rule
read everything from archon.model.finding
read everything from archon.model.report
read everything from archon.engine.scanner
read everything from archon.rules.catalog

!!! The target kind implied by a path's extension.
kind-of receives path as text returns text begin paragraph
    when ny.lang.text::ends_with with s being path, suffix being ".matrix" then
        give "matrix"
    otherwise when ny.lang.text::ends_with with s being path, suffix being ".mat" then
        give "matrix"
    otherwise
        give "code"
    end when
end paragraph

!!! Scan one path and print its findings and report. Returns the finding count,
!!! or -1 when the path could not be read.
scan-path receives path as text returns number begin paragraph
    value contents is read_text with path being path
    consider contents
        when Result.Ok holding source then
            value kind is kind-of with path being path
            value rules is rules-for with kind being kind
            value target is build scan-target with label being path, kind being kind, content being source
            value findings is scan with target being target, rules being rules
            repeat for each item in findings
                say (finding-summary with item being item)
            end repeat
            value summary is summarize with target being target, findings being findings, rules-applied being (the length of rules)
            say (report-summary with summary being summary)
            give the length of findings
        when Result.Error holding message then
            say "error: " plus path plus ": " plus message
            give minus 1
        otherwise
            give minus 1
    end consider
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph
    value count is arg_count with nothing
    when count is less than 1 then
        say "usage: archon <path> [<path> ...]"
        give 2
    end when

    variable failures as number is 0
    repeat for index from 0 to count
        value found is scan-path with path being (arg with index being index)
        when found is less than 0 then
            set failures to failures plus 1
        end when
    end repeat

    when failures is greater than 0 then
        give 1
    end when
    give 0
end paragraph
